; Regression: a statement that is only a discarded operator result used to
; compile clean (2026-08-15).
;
; Scaly has no assignment operator — `=` is equality, and the write is
; `set target: value`. So this pair
;
;     set arr[0]: 111
;     arr[0] = 222
;
; leaves arr[0] at 111, and the second line was accepted with rc 0 and not a
; word. It is what made a broken array WRITE look like a broken array read while
; the real defect (&arr[i] answering the element's value) was being hunted
; elsewhere — see tests/regress/address_of_array_element.scaly.
;
; Operators are pure by definition in this language, so a discarded operator
; result cannot have had a side effect: the statement is provably dead, not
; merely suspicious.
;
; xfail: the result of operator '=' is discarded

var arr int[4]
arr[0] := 111
arr[0] = 222
if arr[0] <> 222
    exit 1
print "unreachable"
